# EXPECT: over an iterable that is not provably numeric
# ouroboros#198: a loop-scoped for binder (here: interrogated, in a function)
# is a C double block-local, so its iterable must provably yield numbers.
# This string-literal iterable built and died at RUN time with the AOT's own
# "non-numeric value in a numeric context" where the VM prints a null b a;
# now refused by name at build time. Numeric controls: t225/t228 (literal
# numeric lists), DMG (`for i in range of N` over a module-bound name).
define f(q) as:
    for r in ["a", "b"]:
        print of r
        print of (prev of r)
    return 0
f of 1
